    "type": "bugfix",
    "problem": [
      {
        "text": "All eight EXL3 compilation units included ../exl3_gemv_kernel.cuh, but that header is absent from the parent quant directory.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_caba958e06714184894e4dddf9bd22ee",
          "call_053aee6e5f63486e8c51ed7ac9c0a7bf"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "reasoning": [
      {
        "text": "Removing the stale include addresses the missing-header dependency rather than supplying a GEMV implementation. The existing GEMM header and per-unit declarations remain included.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_9b8cdc13c5444cc2a08e9d7ef06a0c35",
          "call_7065fa7b9d5547918a252c4c5f14d208"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "impact": [
      {
        "text": "This removes a source-level compilation obstacle from the extension build: setup.py recursively collects .cu files, including these units. Successful compilation of the complete extension is not established.",
        "basis": "inference",
        "evidence": [
          "call_c7ee56d7813a4543a7afc1770f1085a5",
          "call_caba958e06714184894e4dddf9bd22ee",
          "call_053aee6e5f63486e8c51ed7ac9c0a7bf"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "source_notes": [
      {
        "text": "Issue #21, \u201cBuild Failure on Windows: CUDA 12.4 / PyTorch 2.7.0+cu126 / VS 2022,\u201d reports errors in PyTorch/CUDA headers and was closed without a solution. It does not report this missing GEMV header; it is not evidence that this change resolves that issue.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_6cfaf23d3b6b4fd1a725496263c5f2ae"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "limitations": [
      "No CUDA compilation or runtime test was performed. This include-only change offers no useful numerical computation to validate with a scalar Python model."
    ],
    "links": [],
    "chapters": [
      {
        "id": "quantized-inference",
        "title": "Remove the stale GEMV header dependency",
        "claims": [
          {
            "text": "The complete change deletes the same include from exl3_comp_unit_1.cu through exl3_comp_unit_8.cu; it changes no kernel bodies, dispatch entries or numerical constants.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_9b8cdc13c5444cc2a08e9d7ef06a0c35",
              "call_bc70cc60713e4213a005419a153360f4",
              "call_909a84a6fc5a44c3931511a9e5edb023",
              "call_954af5adbb5443c2b74096dcc5d22b68",
              "call_e72b87e50354431fae4b387fd2c966a4",
              "call_1b6b3758cefc425282ff002865d0b4ea",
              "call_43cd65fa19144fd28ae41ff8fff27be1",
              "call_5c2966b07ace4290b956cd9161912730"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The inspected first unit defines FP32 and FP16 GEMM function-pointer arrays using EXL3_GEMM_KERNEL_INSTANCES. Its GEMM implementation include remains intact. Whole-parent search finds exl3_gemv only in the eight removed include directives, supporting deletion rather than replacement as the narrowly scoped repair.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_7065fa7b9d5547918a252c4c5f14d208",
              "call_caba958e06714184894e4dddf9bd22ee",
              "call_9b8cdc13c5444cc2a08e9d7ef06a0c35"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "findings": [],
    "summary": "Removes references to an absent GEMV header from all eight EXL3 compilation units, leaving GEMM code and dispatch unchanged."
